  "int-chg-west": {
   "_why": "R-INT-01 CHG_INT: from the U5 column via to U4 IO15 (pad 26). Every way south from U5 is walled in on F.Cu (SYS pour, C4/C11), In2 (SW island, Pack+ V) and B.Cu (TS pair, BAT+); the only clean way round is the west end. Found with a zone-aware 3-layer A* (scratch pcb_path3.py: fills of non-GND nets are obstacles, L1 +0.15/0.3 kept out, footprint keepouts honoured) at 0.12 mm clearance: B.Cu north-west round U5 and south under the module body 3 mm east of the antenna keepout (x 6.3). The A* 0.05 mm jog at (12.3-12.65, 46.45) became a 0.35 mm east step at y 46.10, passing 0.47 mm north of the +3.1V via at (12.14,46.92); the x 9.3 leg cannot move east (BAT+). 2026-10-21 split from the expander line: under the module the B.Cu turns east at y 55.48 (0.48 mm north of the pad-61 GND vias, south of the UART pair's diagonals), passes under the UART TX run at y 56.23 to one via at (19.05,56.23) in the F.Cu pocket between ePaper BUSY and pads 22-27, and enters pad 26 from the west (pcb_path3 found the same corridor at 0.15 mm). The old tail (F.Cu/In2 hops at y 61.9, 2 vias) is gone.",
